    "explanation": "Rider and driver, here is why this case goes to a human reviewer instead of being decided here. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-09115) has a 160-second gap between consecutive fixes, from 20:03:10 to 20:05:50 SGT, and that gap sits inside the very stretch of route the rider disputes. A gap of more than 90 seconds inside the disputed segment makes the trace impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07(a); its admissibility carries issue code GPS_GAP at weight_multiplier 0.6, so it is also discounted under POL-GEN-02(2). That matters in two ways. First, the 4.0 km excess (15.0 km traced against the 11.0 km booked optimal, 36.4%) is carried by this one artifact, so my confidence in any merits ruling is capped at 0.6, below the platform floor of 0.70, and POL-RD-10(1) fires. Second, because the trace is impaired, POL-RD-07(ii) says a deviation may not be established on the trace alone and must be carried by an independent source.\n\nI checked every independent source the policy names and none exists. The chat log (EV-CHAT-09115) contains no admission of a detour: the driver's only message says his navigation display refreshed and he continued toward the destination. The fare breakdown (EV-FARE-09115) charges no ERP gantries (SGD 0.00), so nothing places the vehicle on a corridor the optimal route does not use. The driver's statement denies an extra stop and a detour request and does not admit the route. And trip_record.actual_distance_km (15.0 km) is a rounded copy of the same trace measurement, which POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-07(ii) both exclude.\n\nWith the trace impaired and no independent corroboration, POL-RD-07(iii) and POL-RD-10(3) require ESCALATE rather than NO_ACTION, because this gap in the proof is a data failure and not a finding for the driver. The disputed SGD 5.80 is therefore held, not collected and not refunded.\n\nFor transparency, had the trace been clean the arithmetic would have given a PARTIAL_REFUND: charged_total SGD 26.60, less a recomputed fare of SGD 20.8310 — (3.80 + 0.75 x 11.0 km + 0.28 x 22 min) = 18.21, surged at the recorded 1.1 multiplier to 20.031, plus the 0.80 platform fee, with no ERP, no fixed surcharge, no waiting fee and no promo — leaving SGD 5.7690, rounded up to SGD 5.80, which is 21.7% of the charge (below the 90% full-refund share) and above the SGD 0.50 de minimis.\n\nOn the points both sides raised: there is no repeat-deviation pattern (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 610 completed trips in 90 days), so no POL-RD-06 pattern is established, no balance is resolved against the driver, and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral follows. No traffic advisory covers the corridor — EV-ADVIS-09115-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT), so POL-RD-03 exonerates nothing and cannot be tested in either direction. No rider-requested detour or relocation is on the record: both chat waypoint_hints are null and the pickup and dropoff amendment fields are null, so POL-RD-04 and POL-RD-05 are not engaged. And there is no pass-through or billing-integrity correction: ERP, tolls, airport surcharge and waiting-time fee are all SGD 0.00, so POL-RD-09 yields nothing and no POL-RD-09(4) referral arises. Finally, even taken at face value the excess (4.0 km, 36.4%) clears the two POL-RD-01 establishment tests but not its materiality tests (over 50% or over 8.0 km), so POL-RD-06 is not triggered on this trip.\n\nWhat would resolve this for the reviewer: an independent record of the vehicle's path across the 160-second gap — a traffic advisory covering that corridor, an off-corridor ERP crossing, or an admission of the route from either party."
